      "writtenOn": "2025-04-14T18:17:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The SkPaint shading logic when there\u0027s an SkShader is a little convoluted due to history. If there\u0027s a regular SkShader, the RGB of the paint color are ignored, but it gets modulated by the paint alpha:\n\n    sk_sp\u003cSkShader\u003e srcShader \u003d SkShaders::Color(paint.getColor4f(), /*cs\u003d*/nullptr);;\n    if (paint.getShader()) {\n       srcShader \u003d SkShaders::Blend(SkBlendMode::kDstIn, std::move(srcShader), paint.refShader());\n    }\n    srcShader \u003d srcShader-\u003emakeWithColorFilter(paint.refColorFilter());\n    sk_sp\u003cSkImageFilter\u003e srcColor \u003d SkImageFilters::Shader(std::move(srcShader), paint.isDither() ? Dither::kYes : Dither::kNo);\n    \nThis uses a Blend to mix the paint color with any shader. The kDstIn mode multiplies the src color by the dst alpha channel. *edit*: your PS11 still uses Compose, which wouldn\u0027t show the paint alpha making things transparent. I also don\u0027t think we should do a src color blend CF-IF to get the solid color mixed with the coverage mask (not sure if that shows up or if src will discard that entirely).\n\nIt\u0027s also a subtle difference, but applying the SkColorFilter to the Shader means there\u0027s one image filter node that produces one image output that includes the CF effects. With your code, we\u0027d produce an image of just the shader, and then process that by the CF-IF.  That has logic to defer applying the CF until it needs to, so it wouldn\u0027t necessarily create a second intermediate output, it would just apply the CF automatically when sampling the shader\u0027s output into the next step. Since that is just a blend with the lighting equations calculated by the coverage blur, it\u0027s not being sampled multiple times so I wouldn\u0027t expect a performance impact, but adjusting the CF to be handled in the first step makes that more explicit.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 163,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 165,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "b6c1119f8dcc86fed5ad77c8650a9b89f54af0b4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
